     3	1. **Round-one findings still open.** Prove ordered IDs and text through both real entry points, including an excluded article. Use each invocation’s cutoff for the judge. V2 specifies September 20, but the slice ends July 7. The 6,000-attempt allowance is a valid stop if intentional, but it is not a worst-case retry bound. A format retry can itself make three network attempts. The cited astra wrapper also omits the shared ledger. The new wrapper must preserve reservation and stop enforcement on every attempt. Finally, triage promises a first-scored-week checkpoint that v2 does not contain. The judge’s recent-history rule still admits all qualifying new arrivals, so it does not bound request size. Add a stored-data size check and a late-stage monitoring threshold. [V2 launcher and slice](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:141) · [Format retry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/runner.py:323) · [Network retry](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1/live.py:82) · [Astra wrapper](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-6/gate1-candidate/gate1_candidate.py:94) · [Triage checkpoint](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/triage-1.md:15) · [Judge evidence selection](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:41)
     4	
     5	2. **The two decisions.** **Count independently eligible financial matters in `N`.** D665 counts every listed matter, and D431 compares the products as configured. D505 still says the new system should use the company’s own figures as evidence. The blind list must therefore distinguish a worthwhile question from a figure worth filing. Print the subgroup so Alex can see how much of the result comes from that policy. **The sealed-replay exception needs an explicit decision.** D613 describes what its Step 1 census checked. It does not define “unread” for either system. Exempt a sealed replay only where the record supports ordinary replay use. An article can inform tuning without being named in a decision. Query structured archives and traces, including binary and ignored files, and require a known-hit control. `rg -F -f` alone cannot establish absence. [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9410) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795) · [D505](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5835) · [D613](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8197) · [V2 census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:42)
     6	
     7	3. **The reading can still move the verdict.** `council_mark.py` is tied to Deck 1 and asserts **19 cards**. Its support marks also lack a distinct *insufficient* value. Provide a comparison input and freeze how missing answers, insufficient evidence, disputes, and duplicate questions enter each denominator and minimum. Require an explicit rejection on every plant. V2’s wording could let “cannot tell” slip through as a plant that was never accepted. Freeze what happens if a week has fewer than 40 eligible articles. [Deck builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/pilot-deck-1/council-marking/council_mark.py:60) · [Allowed marks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/pilot-deck-1/council-marking/council_mark.py:132) · [V2 credit and controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:114) · [Sampling](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:72)
     8	
     9	4. **Monitoring still lacks the denominator for its stop.** Settled attempts include retries and failed sends. The attempt log is also best-effort. It cannot supply completed clean articles for the 2× rule. Add completed-article and completed-judge-day progress, then compare each component with its own baseline. The Step 1 slice baseline is rebased, but it cannot price late judging. Keep D449’s explicit redo authorization. A stopped ledger does not by itself authorize six fresh draws. [V2 monitor](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:239) · [Attempt log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:99) · [D449](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4937) · [D666 scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9443)
    10	
    11	5. **Required reports still differ from D665.** D400 line 5 needs all three passes. The date check is agreement across all three sends for at least 90% of eligible **questions**, not agreement in 90% of passes. The July frozen-reference readout needs both systems and the unseeded question mapping, not Stage B on the new system alone. Step 2’s old method needs reference counterparts, merge judgments, and the no-merge detail comparison. Name those inputs before launch. The two source-based floors remain explicitly unmeasured. Get agreement on that reporting gap before the run. [V2 check table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v2.md:156) · [D400 accounting](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/accounting.py:188) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795) · [Step 2 method](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:305)
    12	
    13	**NOT READY: prove identical inputs and cutoff through both launchers, settle the exposure exception, freeze the comparison reader and scorer, and make the required checks and monitoring executable.**4756:## D428 · 2026-11-11 · Stage B's lines compare figure and yes/no questions apart with the baseline
6728:  the 40 July topics are the council's scaled diagnostic, not his numbers; (2) Stage B on D428's lines, not passed; (3) the
  4756	## D428 · 2026-11-11 · Stage B's lines compare figure and yes/no questions apart with the baseline
  4757	
  4758	- **Asked:** "第二段（让老判断程序每天去判新系统自己出的题）怎么算通过？基准里老程序在人工写的题上：数字题站不住 8%，是非题 0%，16 道题最后一天全部站得住。"
  4759	  - Options: compare figure and yes/no questions apart (recommended): "数字题站不住的比例不超过基准再加 5 个百分点（约 13%–14%）；是非题不超过 5%；三轮共约 30 道题里，最后一天站不住的不超过 3 道，“证据不足”的另外列出。不看总体比例，因为总体会随题型比例变化。代价：判断程序没变差时，数字题这条也有 6%–17% 的机会被误判不过。"; apart with 10 points; the design's original lines (overall 8%, last at least 90%).
  4760	  - Alex: "数字题和是非题分开比 (Recommended)".
  4761	- **Decided:** Stage B passes when, over its three draws, (1) the share of decided figure-question judgements that are
  4762	  UNSUPPORTED is at most 5 points above the baseline's (4 of 52 with the unresolved left out, 7.7%; 5 of 53 counted
  4763	  against, 9.4%: so at most 12.7% to 14.4% on the same three readings); (2) the share of decided yes/no judgements that are
  4764	  UNSUPPORTED is at most 5%; (3) of the judged theses whose last judgement in the window is decided, at most 3 in 30 (scaled
  4765	  to the number judged) are UNSUPPORTED, with the INSUFFICIENT last judgements reported beside. No overall line. The
  4766	  design's other lines (no draw incomplete after one redo; nine in ten laddered theses judged at least once; the control
  4767	  theses) and its NOT MEASURED conditions stand. Baseline: `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/RESULT.md`; the lines'
  4768	  chance behaviour: `stage_b/result/line-chance.txt`.
  4769	- **Scope:** the clean path's Step 4, Stage B.

codex
**V3 fixes the main launch requirements, but it can still declare a winner from an unfinished comparison.** If a replay stops in August, v3 lets its August snapshot compete with the other system’s September output. D665 calls for three draws of each system at the frozen cutoff. [V3 incomplete-draw rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:129) · [D665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9410)

1. **Unfinished draws and separate ledgers — gap.** Return partial draws to Alex as diagnostics, with no release verdict. Separating charges by system is workable, but letting the other system continue after a final stop changes D449’s whole-run stop and D666’s shared guard. Keep the shared stop or record an explicit replacement. [V3 run rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:201) · [D449](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4937) · [D666](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9443)

2. **Input parity, cutoff, retries and astra — resolved in design.** V3 requires ordered ID and text parity through both entry points, invocation-specific judge cutoffs, and astra checks on retries with the shared stop and reservations intact. The freeze review should exercise those requirements, including a trailing day without articles. [Input proof](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:72) · [Limits, astra and cutoff](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:144)

3. **Exposure and financial matters — one gap.** The search scope, binary handling, source-copy exclusions and controls are specified. The exemption is still too broad. A `replay.py` run can be a development experiment. Require evidence of ordinary production use before exempting its reads. D613 only established what appeared in new-system Step 1 traces. The company-figure flag and inclusion in `N` are resolved. A1 determines whether a matter warrants its own question. D505 still governs what the new system opens. [V3 exposure rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:48) · [D613](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8197) · [V3 financial flag](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:81) · [D505](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5835)

4. **Cards, controls and scoring — one gap.** The common card format, sample, short-week rule, distinct support marks and explicit plant rejection are specified. The guardrail changes **unsupported** to **not supported**, counting insufficient and absent answers as unsupported. That can reverse the verdict. Use D665’s unsupported share, report the other categories separately, and freeze which eligible marks count toward the subgroup minimum. [V3 scoring and controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:109) · [Card builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:158) · [D665 guardrails](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:9415) · [D428 denominators](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4761)

5. **Monitoring and required reports — one gap.** Completed-work counts, like-with-like comparison and D449’s redo requirement are specified. V3 still cannot catch all sibling draws overspending together, and “size found” does not say whether to stop at the observed maximum or a stated ceiling. Freeze an absolute late-stage stop alongside the sibling check. The versions manifest, D428 limits, illustrative statistics, D400’s three-pass reporting, D431 for both systems, and Step 2 checks are restored in design. Record council agreement on the two unmeasured floors as planned. [V3 monitoring](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:255) · [Size proxy](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:174) · [Manifest](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:35) · [Reports](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:138) · [Checks and floors](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v3.md:165)

**NOT READY: require complete draws for a release verdict, reconcile the split ledgers with the shared-stop decision, narrow the replay exemption by actual use, restore the unsupported-answer denominator, and freeze an absolute late-stage stop.**
